WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.100
Although designed for federal environments,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.300
NIST SP 800-53 is frequently used outside government.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:11.300
Many organizations use the catalog as a reference for building mature security and privacy programs.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.900
Organizations often map controls to internal policies, customer requirements,

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.900
regulatory obligations, and other frameworks.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.700
This mapping helps teams translate broad security goals into specific control expectations.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:26.100
Commercial adoption happens because the catalog is comprehensive and well understood.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.900
It gives organizations a common way to discuss safeguards even when formal

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.900
federal compliance is not required.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.100
Using the catalog outside government still requires judgment.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.500
Teams should adapt the controls to their mission, systems, resources, laws,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.700
and risk environment.
